---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="About & corrections"
  description="How GamifyPlayer sources information, verifies builds, and accepts corrections."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <h1>About GamifyPlayer</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width: 72ch">
    We are an independent English-language static site aimed at overseas players who want <strong>one answer per page</strong>, with honest version metadata instead of SEO filler.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    <li>Every guide lists <strong>build / patch</strong>, <strong>last verified date</strong>, and <strong>platform scope</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Briefings summarize <strong>official channels</strong> or widely available streams — we do not host leaked binaries, unreleased footage, or datamined strings.
    </li>
    <li>Tools stay in <strong>low-risk</strong> territory: checklists, calendars, calculators — no automation, no memory injection, no rebroadcasting of protected map tiles.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width: 72ch">
    Found a regression after a patch? Email <a href="mailto:corrections@gamifyplayer.example">corrections@gamifyplayer.example</a> with the guide URL, your platform, and a screenshot or build
    string from the in-game settings screen. We batch-verify on weekends.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics & search</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width: 72ch">
    Cloudflare Web Analytics loads only when <code>PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN</code> is present. Pagefind runs as a post-step (<code>npm run build:search</code>) so search stays static-friendly.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
